<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · river</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ticino River</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ticino">Ticino</a> is a river that rises in the Swiss <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alps">Alps</a>, flows through the canton of Ticino and Lake Maggiore, and then runs south through <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lombardy">Lombardy</a> to join the Po just below Pavia. Its lower course formed a frontier between Lombardy and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/piedmont">Piedmont</a>, and in 218 BCE <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hannibal">Hannibal</a> defeated the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roman-empire">Romans</a> in a cavalry battle near its banks.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ticino-river.jpg" alt="Ticino River" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Ruaro Matteo · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Twilight_of_the_old_ways.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
